            "review_text": "katanankes\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam90 contributions\n0\nGood Japanese fried food\nApr 2016 • Solo\nVisited Imotaro for lunch. They sport a large selection of lunch sets that are very good value for money. Their specialty seems to be deep fried food: not tempura, but tonkatsu (cutlet) and similar \"furai\" dishes (if I am not mistaken furai means fried) such as oysters, chicken, beef, etc. \n\nI had beef cheese croquettes that were meaty (four) and tasty. They came with the usual myso soup, rice, some salad and pickles. For 7 dollars a reasonable deal.\n\nDo not be put off by the small entrance, inside the place is actually fairly large, with a room with big booths (each good for a party of six, or maybe more if you are slim) and a room in the upper level. \n\nThey also have shabu shabu (Japanese hot pot) and a vast selection of drinks. Please, be warned that this is NOT a sushi restaurant, sushi selection is almost non existent. \n\nWholeheartedly recommended for lunch.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten April 22, 2016",
